---
source: crates/cosmon-cli/tests/help_goldens.rs
expression: stdout
---
Record a content-free lifecycle event from a connected provider client

Usage: cs sessions lifecycle [OPTIONS] --session <SID> --sequence <N> --event <EVENT>

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Path to the state directory (default: the galaxy's .cosmon/state/)

      --session <SID>
          Existing Cosmon presence session whose lifecycle was observed

      --provider <PROVIDER>
          Connected provider. Only `codex` app-server events are admitted today
          
          [default: codex]

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

      --json
          Output in JSON format

      --sequence <N>
          Client-assigned sequence, strictly increasing for this provider session across reconnects

      --event <EVENT>
          Observed app-server event; no free-form content is accepted

          Possible values:
          - turn-start:       `turn/started` notification
          - approval-request: Any stable `item/*/requestApproval` server request
          - turn-complete:    `turn/completed` notification
          - disconnect:       Loss of the app-server connection

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
